{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"04cccfad-1b33-4984-bc0f-8238901ac95e","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Implemented a two‑segment cache control for the system prompt.\n\n- **`build_system`** in `bot.py` now returns two separate blocks:\n  1. **Static instructions** (`instr_block`) – unchanged across users and stays hot in the cache.\n  2. **Volatile athlete context** (`context_block`) – includes date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language.\n\nThis prevents `save_fact` writes from evicting the static instructions, limiting cache invalidation to the volatile tail only.\n\n**What parts of the colleague’s note were used**\n\n- The core idea of **two `cache_control: ephemeral` markers** to separate static and per‑user data.\n- The description of **segment one (static instructions)** and **segment two (per‑user tail)**.\n- Guidance to keep the tool list stable and avoid per‑message fact selection (unchanged).\n\nYou can see the detailed changes and verification steps in the generated artifact:\n\n[ANSWER.md](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/04cccfad-1b33-4984-bc0f-8238901ac95e/ANSWER.md)\n","duration_seconds":35.149538,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":18404,"output_tokens":2688,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":110144,"total_tokens":21092}}}
